# ported-from-theme.manifest - agora_transparency - the OTHER direction of D-028.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS, AND WHY IT IS NOT THE SIBLING'S MANIFEST WITH THE NAMES SWAPPED.
#
# `agora_theme` carries tests/bin/shared-invariants.manifest, which records the files it
# copied FROM this repository, plus a detector for local edits and, since D-063, one that
# reads this repository over the API. That machinery has a signed decision behind it
# (D-028), a named set of five invariants, and three layers of guard.
#
# Files travel the other way too, and until this file existed NOTHING in this repository
# knew it. tests/bin/executable-bit and tests/bin/preflight were both authored in the theme
# and ported here on 2026-09-06, in a commit whose own subject says so - "the template gets
# the two guardrails the theme has" - and that sentence in a commit message was the entire
# provenance record. A commit message is not a mechanism: it is read once, by the person
# who wrote it.
#
# ⚠️ AND THE HANDED LIST WAS ONE SHORT, WHICH IS THE MOST USEFUL THING ON THIS PAGE.
# Two files were reported as the ports. There are THREE. tests/bin/packaged-claims was
# written here on 2026-09-21 at 10:49 and shares 65 lines of 45 characters or more with the
# theme's tests/bin/claims-match-readme, which was committed at 09:44 the same morning -
# sixty-five minutes earlier. Only 2 of those 65 lines exist in this repository's own
# earlier tests/bin/claims-match-sources, so 63 of them arrived from the theme rather than
# being this project's house style flowing back.
#
# HOW THE THIRD ONE WAS FOUND, because the method is worth more than the file. Every script
# in both tests/bin/ directories was compared against every script in the other by counting
# shared literal lines of 45 characters or more - 38 files against 20, both directions, all
# pairs. That produces a BAND, and reading the band is the whole technique:
#
#   15-24 shared lines   the house style. The contract block, the house-rules paragraph,
#                        the I-028 sentence. Two files written here by the same hand score
#                        in this range (no-key-material against no-patches: 24).
#   37-65 shared lines   real shared substance: helper functions, argument parsers, whole
#                        printed paragraphs.
#
# Nine pairs scored above the band. Eight of them involve a theme file that ORIGINATED HERE
# - no-secrets, no-patches, gate-a-theme.sh and so on - so the shared substance is this
# repository's own, measured on its way back. Exactly one pair had a theme file that is
# genuinely the theme's AND older than its counterpart here: packaged-claims against
# claims-match-readme, 65.
#
# DIRECTION IS SETTLED BY TIMESTAMP, NEVER BY READING THE CODE. Two files that share 65
# lines tell you they are related; they do not tell you which way. `git log --reverse` on
# both paths does, and it is the only thing that does:
#
#   executable-bit       theme 2026-09-06T13:04:44   here 2026-09-06T15:14:49   (+2h10m)
#   preflight            theme 2026-09-06T12:42:31   here 2026-09-06T15:14:49   (+2h32m)
#   claims-match-readme  theme 2026-09-21T09:44:30   here 2026-09-21T10:49:01   (+1h05m)
#
# The same method run against the eight files the theme's own manifest records puts this
# repository first in every one of them, which is the control: a method that said "theme
# first" for everything would be measuring nothing.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FIELDS, in order. THERE ARE SEVEN, AND THE SIBLING'S MANIFEST HAS SIX.
#
#   script         basename inside tests/bin/ HERE
#   role           invariant | preflight
#   status         verbatim | adapted
#   local_sha256   sha256 of the copy in THIS repository, as it stands now
#   source_path    the path in `agora_theme` the copy was taken from
#   source_sha256  sha256 of the blob at source_path at source_commit
#   source_commit  the `agora_theme` commit the copy was taken from
#
# ⚠️ `source_path` IS THE ADDED FIELD AND IT IS NOT TIDINESS. The theme's manifest derives
# the source path from the basename, because no file it copied was ever renamed. In this
# direction one was: packaged-claims came from claims-match-readme. A six-field manifest
# could not record that record at all - it would have to ask the API for
# tests/bin/packaged-claims in `agora_theme`, get an honest 404, and report broken
# provenance about a file whose provenance is fine. So the path is recorded rather than
# computed, and the two records where it happens to equal the basename are written out in
# full anyway: a field that is usually derivable is a field somebody derives.
#
# WHY EVERY RECORD IS `adapted`, and why that is the expected state here rather than a
# backlog. Measured against the recorded source, not estimated:
#
#   executable-bit    +64/-32     161 source lines -> 193 here
#   preflight         +275/-210   737 source lines -> 802 here
#   packaged-claims   +836/-437   656 source lines -> 1055 here
#
# These are not copies that drifted; they are copies that were REWRITTEN for a different
# subject on arrival. preflight runs the pipeline's lint jobs, and the two pipelines do not
# share a job list - the theme runs stylelint and nightwatch, this package runs phpstan over
# PHP tests and a Drupal CMS install smoke. packaged-claims went further still: the theme's
# guard refuses a figure stated twice IN ONE FILE, and this package's prose is spread over
# six files no reader opens together, so every registered figure here declares a HOME and
# the detector runs over all six. That is a different rule, not a port of the same one.
#
# The consequence for this manifest is that `verbatim` may never appear in it by accident.
# `adapted` asserts local_sha256 != source_sha256, and tests/bin/ported-copies fails a
# record whose status contradicts its own two hashes - which is the check that catches one
# hash being refreshed while the other is not.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THE THREE LAYERS ANSWER, AND WHICH QUESTION EACH CANNOT.
#
#   this file                    what was taken, from where, at which commit
#   tests/bin/ported-copies      has a copy been edited HERE since        (offline, in the gate)
#   tests/bin/ported-drift       has the theme changed it SINCE          (over the API, in the gate)
#
# ⚠️ A CLEAN `ported-copies` RUN DOES NOT MEAN THE COPIES ARE CURRENT. It compares a local
# file against a recorded hash, so it answers "has this been edited here" - truthfully, and
# about a different question than the one that matters. That exact gap is what D-063 was
# signed over: 28 days and 125 genuinely-absent lines accumulated in the theme's
# identity-strings while its detector printed CLEAN, correctly. ported-drift is what asks
# the other question, and it runs on every push with nothing checked out but this tree.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REGENERATING A RECORD, and step one is not optional.
#
#   1. `bash tests/bin/ported-drift` FIRST. It prints, per record, how far the SOURCE has
#      moved since the recorded commit. Read that number before deciding anything: a delta
#      is data, not an instruction, and the theme's own worked example is 132 upstream lines
#      of which 0 should have been taken.
#   2. Decide PER HUNK what belongs here. These three files were adapted on arrival; a hunk
#      that fixes a bug in shared logic belongs here, and a hunk about stylelint does not.
#   3. Re-derive BOTH hashes and read the commit with
#      `git -C <theme checkout> rev-parse HEAD`. Never type a sha, and never carry a hash
#      forward from the line above.
#   4. Re-run ported-drift and confirm the delta moved to exactly what you left behind.
#
# Neither detector has a `--fix` flag. A guard that can silence itself in one keystroke is
# the thing it was built to prevent.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE STATE ON THE DAY THIS FILE WAS WRITTEN, recorded because a first run that is green is
# a claim and this one is a measurement with a date on it.
#
# All three source blobs are byte-identical to `agora_theme`'s 1.x HEAD (bf433c9) right now.
# executable-bit and preflight have sat at a FIFTEEN-DAY-OLD commit, unwatched, and drifted
# by nothing. That is not a lucky result, it is the argument for how the cap is measured:
# tests/bin/ported-drift starts its clock at the first upstream commit that touched the path
# AFTER the recorded one - the moment a drift begins to exist - so these two report 0 days,
# not 15. A cap on the age of the RECORD would have opened this file with two findings
# against two records that are exactly right, which is the fastest way to teach the next
# reader that the check is noise.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REGENERATED 2026-09-21 (T-0619), one record, and the four steps above were followed in order.
#
#   1. tests/bin/ported-drift FIRST: 3 records compared, 3 read, 3 provenance verified,
#      **0 behind** 1.x at a427375, 0 past the cap, 0 findings. So there was nothing upstream to
#      take and no per-hunk decision to make - the change is local adaptation only.
#   2. What changed HERE: packaged-claims gained LICENCE-MANIFEST.md as a seventh packaged
#      subject, four comparisons about it, one source-against-source comparison of
#      AccessibilityTest's DECLARED_PAGES constant, and a second --online block that reads this
#      project's own phpunit trace. None of it came from agora_theme.
#   3. local_sha256 re-derived from the file on disk. source_sha256 and source_commit are
#      UNCHANGED and were not retyped, because step 1 proved the source has not moved - a hash
#      carried forward from the line above is exactly what this manifest exists to catch.
#   4. ported-drift re-run afterwards: same 3 / 3 / 3 / 0 / 0 / 0.
#
# The record stays `adapted`, which it must: ported-copies fails a record whose status
# contradicts its own two hashes, and these two were already 836 lines apart.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REGENERATED AGAIN 2026-09-21 (T-0629), the same one record, same four steps in order.
#
#   1. tests/bin/ported-drift FIRST, and it was run BEFORE the edit was decided rather than
#      to justify it: 3 records compared, 3 read, 3 provenance verified, **0 behind** 1.x,
#      oldest drift 0 days, 0 past the cap, 0 findings, network READ anonymously. So there
#      was nothing upstream to take and no per-hunk decision to make.
#   2. What changed HERE: ONE entry appended to packaged-claims' NOT CHECKED list - the two
#      figures content/MEDIA-LICENCES.md states about `haven`, which are facts about another
#      project at a version that will move and which no offline read can produce. Nothing
#      came from agora_theme and no executable line moved; the list goes 10 -> 11.
#   3. local_sha256 re-derived with `sha256sum` from the file on disk and substituted by
#      command, never typed. source_sha256 and source_commit UNCHANGED and not retyped,
#      because step 1 proved the source has not moved.
#   4. ported-drift re-run afterwards: same 3 / 3 / 3 / 0 / 0 / 0.
#
# ⚠️ D-028 PERMITS THIS AND THE DISTINCTION IS WORTH RESTATING, because the wider version of
# it was invented once and cost six days. What D-028's 2026-08-24 amendment forbids is
# editing a copied invariant to make a red GO AWAY - weakening. It does not forbid editing
# one; option B's own cost line contemplates "one manifest to regenerate whenever a shared
# script legitimately changes", which is this. The edit here makes the guard say MORE about
# what it does not cover, which is the opposite direction from weakening, and the G11 checks
# assert that list is non-empty rather than asserting its length, so nothing was tuned to fit.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
