#
# script            role       status    local_sha256                                                    source_path                     source_sha256                                                    source_commit
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# executable-bit - ported 2026-09-06 in 434e289, role `invariant`, gate-a-wave1.sh G10.
#
# It reads the mode a shebang file is COMMITTED at out of the git index rather than from the
# filesystem, and that is the reason it was worth porting rather than reinventing: on this
# Windows checkout git does not track the executable bit, so `[ -x ]` answers TRUE for a
# file committed 100644 while the Linux runner answers FALSE. The theme paid for that
# lesson - its pipeline 950124 was red for a full push cycle behind a green local gate - and
# this repository got the finished guard instead of the same red.
#
# It was not vacuous on arrival: 2 of the 30 shebang files here were committed 100644.
#
# The +64/-32 is mostly the denominators and the prose around them. Both copies read the
# index; neither reads the filesystem.
executable-bit     invariant  adapted   9c1eeadc656e45af94dca93829d19c136ff3f0cf93a19ac3bacfac3ff0ccc011 tests/bin/executable-bit        e63e842a63211e3c125265e3550dfc5b593cf8dc9667e77cace0bc7ffd465373 82201a6a779f5f9bc6ee7bfe2b9782ef78af2dd4
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# preflight - ported 2026-09-06 in 434e289, role `preflight`, in NEITHER gate runner.
#
# It runs the pipeline's own lint jobs against a rig with the pipeline's own fetched
# configuration, and it needs Docker, which is why it is not in the gate and why its role
# says so. The theme's measurements are the reason it exists at all: eight real phpcs errors
# sat undetected on a branch there, three real stylelint findings turned a pipeline red, and
# eslint had never been attempted at all.
#
# ⚠️ ITS ROLE BUYS IT NO EXEMPTION FROM THE CAP. A copy that is not in the gate is still a
# copy whose source can move, and this is the largest and most actively developed of the
# three, so it is the one most likely to move. Exempting a copy for its role would mean the record
# most likely to need answering is the one nothing asks about.
#
# ⚠️ THE SOURCE COMMIT IS NOT THE COMMIT THAT CREATED THE FILE THERE. preflight was born in
# the theme at 43505f2 (12:42) and changed again before the port at 82201a6 (13:04), which
# is the theme's HEAD at the moment of copying and therefore what is recorded. The blob at
# 43505f2 hashes to 5201a2cc..., which is NOT what was taken. Recording the birth commit
# because it is the one a reader would guess at would have produced a record that fails its
# own hash check.
preflight          preflight  adapted   2ee82b86c175440c3086596a3011877889565e00a5932b3a4c415f5db35a88a3 tests/bin/preflight             054957aefaa94bb5ab3b697f94b956fd01a946a9bd3bf5d0685141371d4b982f 82201a6a779f5f9bc6ee7bfe2b9782ef78af2dd4
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# packaged-claims - written 2026-09-21 in d7cd919, role `invariant`, gate-a-wave1.sh G11.
# THE RENAMED ONE, and the record this manifest's seventh field exists for.
#
# Its own header cites the theme's guard and argues about it, which is what made the
# relationship look like a citation rather than a port. It is both: the argument is real and
# so are the 63 lines. What crossed is the machinery - the argument parser, `fatal`,
# `not_read`, the colour constants, the word-to-number table, the compare-and-print helper,
# the NOT CHECKED apparatus and several printed paragraphs verbatim. What did not cross is
# the rule: the theme refuses a figure stated twice in one file, and this one gives every
# registered figure a HOME across six packaged files.
#
# ⚠️ A CITATION IN A HEADER IS NOT A PROVENANCE RECORD, and this file is the whole reason to
# say so. packaged-claims names `agora_theme`'s guard nine times and a reader would call
# that well-documented. None of those nine mentions records WHICH COMMIT, so none of them
# can be checked, and no mechanism could ever tell you the source had moved. That is the
# difference between prose about provenance and provenance.
packaged-claims    invariant  adapted   33f5fa0477294ebfb1510b1e7d15e1dacb316b6bbe59d73803f67a098c40ff71 tests/bin/claims-match-readme   fe3b22f1d644a78108296d93209c8930297db4c2e2af380b385892c4497a7891 d8079ad0aeb63bafb992cab31b37dcc2818f3ce3
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWO SOURCE COMMITS, DECLARED RATHER THAN COUNTED. tests/bin/ported-copies carries its own
# independent copy of the distinct source commits above and compares the two sets, so a
# half-finished re-sync - some records moved forward, some left behind, every individual
# record still telling the truth about itself - fails, because the SET stops matching the
# declaration. A manifest can be internally consistent and collectively wrong.
#
# WHAT NOTHING HERE CAN SEE, named rather than left to be discovered: a FOURTH file ported
# from the theme with no record in this file at all. The closed-world check below compares
# this manifest against a list declared in ported-copies, so a record deleted from here
# fails - but a port that was never recorded in either place is invisible to both. Finding
# the third one took a full cross-product of two tests/bin/ directories and a reading of
# both git histories; that is a task for a person, and it is written down here so the next
# person knows what it costs rather than assuming a green gate covered it.
